  "summary": "@worca/app 1.14.0-rc.4: keyword co-occurrence in agent/bridge code, no traced installer harm",
  "details": "Package ships an agent/coding-assistant app with a browser extension (sidebar bundles for Chrome/Edge/Firefox), a bridge server (src/core/bridge/server.mjs), an egress policy and proxy (src/core/egress-policy.mjs, src/core/egress-proxy.mjs), a platform heartbeat (src/core/platform-heartbeat.mjs), and workspace detectors. Pattern rules fired on keyword co-occurrence of 'ping'/'curl'/'POST'/'hostname'/'GET' across these files, which are expected tokens for an egress-control subsystem, a heartbeat/health module, and workspace language detectors (code.mjs references language ids). A PATH reference in src/core/skills.mjs sits alongside a '/.claude/skills/' path and is consistent with locating per-user skill directories rather than mutating shell PATH. No hardcoded non-first-party exfiltration endpoint, no credential-store read (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, browser secret stores), no install/import-time fetch-and-execute, no obfuscated destination, and no lifecycle-script dropper are evident in the scanned surface. The static matches are the generic shape of an egress proxy and heartbeat subsystem, not a traced attack path.",
